 "sentences": [
  "There was a spring of light at the foot of a hill.",
  "Old Wen sat on a stone nearby.",
  "A clay jar glowed beside it.",
  "A smooth hollow lay open in the rock.",
  "A spiral shell lay on the slope.",
  "A boulder sat on the slope.",
  "Ada wanted to send a boat into the sky.",
  "She pushed the hollow hard, but it did not move.",
  "She moved the shell, and it settled into the hollow.",
  "\"What belongs in the hollow?\" Ada asked Wen.",
  "\"The carved boat belongs in the hollow,\" Wen said.",
  "Ada was delighted with the shell.",
  "She wondered what the shell did.",
  "She moved the shell again, and it came out of the hollow.",
  "She wondered what the hollow needed.",
  "She touched the hollow, but it would not move.",
  "She grew frustrated with the hollow.",
  "She pressed on the boulder, but it did not budge.",
  "She wondered what the boulder needed.",
  "\"What breaks the boulder?\" Ada asked Wen.",
  "\"I don't know what breaks the boulder,\" Wen said.",
  "Ada touched the boulder again, but nothing happened.",
  "She grew frustrated with the boulder.",
  "She shook the jar, and it went dark.",
  "She was delighted with the jar.",
  "She gave the boulder a hard push, but it did not move.",
  "She moved the shell, and it settled into the hollow.",
  "She shoved the boulder, but it would not move.",
  "Again and again she tried the boulder, the hollow and the jar, but nothing gave.",
  "She felt anxious about the jar.",
  "She pushed the boulder hard, but it did not budge.",
  "\"What fills the jar?\" Ada asked Wen.",
  "\"I don't know what fills the jar,\" Wen said.",
  "Ada gave the boulder a hard push again, but nothing happened.",
  "She shook the jar, but it did not move.",
  "She grew frustrated with the jar.",
  "She moved the shell, and it came out of the hollow.",
  "She pressed on the boulder, but it would not move.",
  "She shoved the boulder, but it did not budge.",
  "She dipped the jar into the spring, and it began to glow.",
  "She was delighted with the jar.",
  "She dipped the jar into the spring again, but nothing happened.",
  "She pushed the boulder hard.",
  "But this time the boulder split apart.",
  "A little carved boat lay among the pieces.",
  "A heap of pebbles lay on the ground.",
  "Ada realized that the boulder moved only if the jar began to glow.",
  "She was delighted with the carved boat.",
  "She moved the carved boat, and it settled into the hollow.",
  "\"What moves the carved boat?\" Ada asked Wen.",
  "\"I don't know what moves the carved boat,\" Wen said.",
  "Ada touched the hollow.",
  "A small skiff took shape beside the hollow.",
  "Ada realized that Wen had been right.",
  "\"What lifts the skiff?\" Ada asked Wen.",
  "\"I don't know what lifts the skiff,\" Wen said.",
  "Ada pushed the skiff hard, and it rose into the air and came down on the far hill.",
  "The carved boat came out of the hollow.",
  "Ada laughed with joy.",
  "She felt anxious about the skiff."
 ],
